      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Simple Sequence Repeat (SSR) markers are one of the most frequently used molecular markers in studies of crop diversity and population structure. This is due to their uniform distribution in the genome, the high polymorphism, reproducibility, and codominant character. Additional advantages are the possibility of automatic analysis and simple interpretation of the results. The M13 tagged PCR reaction significantly reduces the costs of analysis by the automatic genetic analyzers. Here, we also disclose a short protocol of SSR data analysis."},
